<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A sentient ink pen that created itself out of nothing. The pen knowns nothing of what came before the day it had it's first thought&#8212;&quot;body&quot;. It recalls the painful process by which it pulled matter out of the air to create the pen-body in which holds its mind. The God Pen looks like a regular high value ink pen. However when someone tries to write with it, the only thing they write is what the pen is thinking at the time. The person trying to write with it, thinks they are writing what they want to until they put the pen down. Users of the pen express either &quot;euphoric shock&quot; or dysphoria upon realization of the situation. Some even saying the jewel on the top of the pen is so beautiful that they must use it.</p>
<p>Some experiences it has had include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Times of War</li>
<li>Being the Object of Worship by cults</li>
<li>Being helpless to save someone</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> It can think and feel questioning it own existence; it's own uncertainties of it's life and possible death. Millions of pages in 7 different languages document its journeys, it's feelings, people it has met and events it has witnessed. Besides it's discovery during WW2 and it's clinical description the article would include some of it's writings.</p>
<p>It poses very little threat beyond those who are susceptible to the lure of it's &quot;beauty&quot; and those weak minded to be enamored by the &quot;euphoric or dysphoric shock&quot; one can feel after using it. The feeling of euphoria has lead to people making cults surrounding the pen. While the dysphoric feelings have lead to people doing terrible things as they slide into madness. Due to this it is an object that should be contained, in fact it wishes to be contained. Containment should be in a well lit glass case (as the object is afraid of the dark) resting on a rough, yet soft, fabric surface to deter someone from wanting to use it to write with. The walls of the containment unit should also be rough. Due to the painful build up of ink, the object must be used once a week. Also when the pen is engorged with ink people seem to find it harder to resist.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A Ink pen that wrote itself into existences.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Comedic with dark tones. Open to suggestions as I want to make this the best that it can be.</p>

